# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets — first, because everything below is only inconvenient if it leaks.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The Tauri update signing key. Anyone holding it can publish an update that
# every installed copy of Veglass will accept and run. It belongs in a password
# manager, never in a repository — not even a private one, because a private
# repository can be made public by one click and cannot be un-leaked afterwards.
*.key
*.pem
*.p12
*.pfx
.tauri/
src-tauri/*.key
# The public half (`*.key.pub`) is meant to be committed — it goes into
# tauri.conf.json — and the patterns above do not match it, since none of them
# ends the filename. Stated so nobody "fixes" that by widening them.
!*.pub

# Environment files. TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY and TAURI_SIGNING_PRIVATE_KEY_PASSWORD
# live here during a release build; the Gemini API key does not — it is in the
# OS credential store — but a stray one would land here too.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dependencies and build output
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
node_modules/
dist/
dist-ssr/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Rust. `target` holds gigabytes of compiled artefacts and the finished
# installers; `gen` is regenerated from tauri.conf.json on every build.
src-tauri/target/
src-tauri/gen/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local machine noise
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.local
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
ehthumbs.db
$RECYCLE.BIN/

# Editors — keeping the shared recommendations, dropping personal settings.
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Runtime and scratch
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ffmpeg and yt-dlp are fetched at runtime into the app's own data directory,
# never into the repository — but a manual copy dropped here should not be
# committed either: they are tens of megabytes of platform-specific binary.
ffmpeg
ffmpeg.exe
ffprobe
ffprobe.exe
yt-dlp
yt-dlp.exe

# Media and exports, in case anything is tested in place. A repository is the
# wrong place for a two-gigabyte recording.
/media/
/exports/
*.mp4
*.mov
*.mkv
*.webm
*.wav
*.mp3

# Logs and crash reports
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*

# Scratch space
/tmp/
/scratch/
*.tmp
settings.json 
